oments before when we're watching an  episode of Jessie it can be hard to  remember that it's events aren't  happening in real time the actors of the  show don't film the scene in a linear  sequence which can make recreate  every little detail all the more  challenging in season 1 episode 21 Emma  and Zuri asked Jessie if they can watch  an educational movie and she gives them  permission but what Jessie doesn't know  is that the girls are pulling a fast one  on her they use the educational movie  spin as a decoy when really they're  watching a scary doll movie in the  episode titled a dolls outhouse there's  a huge mistake that somehow managed to  make it on to the TV show and that  happens when the girls are watching the  scary movie and Jessie walks in  prompting them to change the channel at  first we can clearly see that Emma and  Zuri are eating popcorn from a bucket  the bucket is half full and some of its  kernels even jump out when Emma gets  scared but moments later Zuri get so  frightened she puts the bucket of  popcorn over her head and not one kernel  falls out it's as if the bucket is  suddenly empty when it was half-full  just seconds ago  [Music]  most TV mistakes occur in episodes but  this general error takes place in the  opening theme song of Jessie at the end  of the catchy tune we see Jessie strut  out of the elevator and meet up with the  rest of the cast outdoors it's a blink  and you'll miss it moment but Jesse's  head passes right through the doorway of  the elevator she looks super tall in  this shot which isn't very accurate  according to home study a residential  elevator can be anywhere between 6 feet  and 8 inches to 8 feet tall and while  Jessie is a fan of wearing high heels  she's really not that tall in real life  [Music]  sure she might look super tall when  standing next to the kid she babysits  but debby Ryan's the actor who plays her  is only 5 foot 6 in real life so it just  doesn't make sense that she would be  taller than an elevator door this  animation mistake caught the eye of  detail-oriented viewers tell us if you  noticed this mistake in the comments one  of the most amazing things to ever  happen on Jessie took place in the  episode titled from the white house to  our house it's in this episode that  Michelle Obama is welcomed onto the  Disney Channel set but that didn't stop  producers from making a handful of  mistakes during this episode in season 3  episode 13 Emma puts together a pep  rally for her school and Ravi is  determined to become the school's new  mascot problem is Luke competes against  his brother for the gig because well if  he wins he'll get to hang out with the  cheerleaders cheerleader is gonna be my  honey a few goofs happen during the pep  rally scene and these mainly revolve  around the applause meter when Ravi  starts rapping the applause meter starts  moving problem is no one in the crowd is  clapping one second the applause meter  is stuck on getting warm and then when  the camera zooms out again it's on hot  viewers pointed out that while Luke  received more applause the meter stated  that Ravi had received more applause  than Luke you may have charisma but I  was born to look goofy in public here  are the things we love talking about old  Disney Channel shows like Jessie if you  have a soft spot for all things Disney  and Nickelodeon be sure to subscribe to  the things and  don't forget to click that Bell and turn  on post notifications so you never miss  another video if you're watching on your  phone or tablet be sure to go into your  YouTube settings and switch on  notifications this way you can be the  first to comment on our latest videos  the pilot episode of Jessie is titled  New york-new nanny and at least the  foundation for the rest of the series  but some of its statements were proved  incorrect by the time the second season  of Jessie made it onto the small screen  it's perfectly normal for pilot episodes  tab continuity errors in them especially  when writers write the pilot episode  before giving the rest of the series  much thought in New york-new nanny  Jessie tells the cab driver soon my dad  who's in the Marine Corps practically  blew his flattop when I told him I was  moving to New York but in season 2  episode 26 it's revealed that her dad is  a lieutenant colonel in the Army  this mistake went unnoticed by viewers  who don't have a military background  however seeing as Jessie was raised in a  military setting it's unlikely that she  would get her father's job title wrong  but that's exactly what happens in the  episode titled GI Jesse the writers of  the show originally intended for JW  Prescott to be in the Marine Corps only  to place him in an entirely different  military branch and it didn't go  unnoticed you talk in a foxhole the  enemy's likely to find you and take you  out in season 4 episode 14 we find out  that the Ross siblings are excited to  attend the win big shindig Suri reveals  that it's her first boy-girl dance  [Music]  and asks Emma for some advice but the  episode titled dance dance resolution is  flawed from the get-go in the opening  scene Jessie pours the kids some orange  juice and sets the pitcher back down on  the table and then something very  mysterious starts happening the pitcher  starts to displace itself between tapes  without anyone ever moving it on top of  that the amount of orange juice in the  pitcher also varies between tanks  clearly the scene wasn't filmed  continuously and producers had a hard  time keeping track of just the pitchers  juice levels these mistakes are easy to  miss considering how hilarious the  opening scene is but once you notice it  you just can't unsee it that's two major  goofs take place in season 1 episode 3  and they're so extreme that they'll have  you wondering how producers miss them in  the first place in the episode titled  used karma Jessie and the kids learn  about Karma and how it can come back to  haunt you so Luke attempts to wash the  karma off of him by standing out in the  rain and cleansing himself when Bertram  first sees Luke his hair is completely  dry and his clothes are wet but not  soaking but then when Bertram walks  through the window to close the blinds  on Luke Luke's hair is completely  drenched and his clothes are dripping  another mistake happens at the end of  the episode when Bertram scares Jessie  and the kids while wearing a cloak he  sits on the couch and reaches over to  grab the remote but then out of nowhere  mr. Kipling can be seen watching TV on  the side table but the coffee table had  been bared just seconds ago I can record  him fish both new york new nanny and a  doll's outhouse are filled with  inconsistencies that can easily be  spotted in retrospect and one of these  continuity errors revolves around Ravi  Ross Ravi spent most of his life in an  orphanage before being adopted by the  Rosses and it's revealed that he had  just been adopted a month before the  pilot episode aired so it makes perfect  sense that Ravi would take his time to  adjust to his new life before attending  school in a dog's outhouse  that he has just been allowed to attend  school for the very first time problem  is this statement is disproved in the  pilot episode of the series in new york  new nanny we see jessie escorting the  kids to the lobby they run out the front  door when their school bus sounds its  horn and it's here that we can clearly  see Ravi waiting for the school bus with  the rest of his siblings so evidently  Ravi had been to school before the  events of a doll's outhouse took place  we mentioned earlier on that there were  a total of three mistakes in the episode  titled the talented mr. Kipling we've  already covered the first one so now  let's find out about the other two oddly  enough these mistakes happen in the very  same scene in this episode Luke and Emma  are paired up together for a photography  assignment and Luke uses his camera to  spy on Bertram who is in his bedroom  shaving his back the first thing viewers  noticed was that Luke's camera isn't  real  this is made obvious by the fact that  the camera doesn't actually have a  screen the second mistake is a  continuity error which is later revealed  in the episode titled the kid whisperer  in this episode Bertram is stunned to  find out that his bedroom has a window  turns out Bertram didn't know he had a  window because of all the clutter on his  windowsill but wait how could Luke have  seen Bertram shaving his back through  the bedroom window if the window had  been overrun by clutter my room doesn't  even have a window we love Emma Ross but  there's something strange about her  interviewee displaying signs of sarcasm  might be a red flag and mainly it's the  fact that she doesn't seem to age like  the other characters do in Jessie emma  is said to be 15 years old for the  majority of the season and her age  doesn't change even though for Christmas  episodes are aired throughout the series  four year run by the end of Jessie emma  is said to be about 17 years old but  then in the spin-off series bunk'd which  takes place after the events of jessie  emma is only 16 years old just marker o  to show the tattoo artists what I want  and that's a wrap on the 10 huge  mistakes that made it into Disney's  Jesse before you go tell us which Jesse  scene made you laugh the most and why in  the comments section below give this  video a big thumbs up and don't forget  to subscribe to the things we'll catch  you next time thanks for watching  [Music]

